  ("(1) El modisto for el modista ‘male fashion designer’ is heard in Spain: todo las separa . . ." 0.0920 0.9081 0.4485 0.4650 0.4647 0.0165 0.0099 0.2744 0.0227)
  ("incluso los modistos (El Mundo, Sp.) ‘everything stands between them . . . even fashion design-" 0.0920 0.9080 0.4650 0.4815 0.4814 0.0165 0.0064 0.3234 0.0566)
  ("ers’. The Academy (DPD, 441) accepts it but Seco and El País reject it. La modista also means" 0.0920 0.9082 0.4815 0.4980 0.4979 0.0165 0.0070 0.3062 0.0356)
  ("‘dressmaker’." 0.0920 0.2088 0.4980 0.5145 0.5145 0.0165 nil 0.3175 0.1169)
  ("(2) In Spain guardias and policías are not the same. The Guardia Civil deals with rural policing," 0.0920 0.9080 0.5267 0.5432 0.5429 0.0165 0.0064 0.2950 0.0225)
  ("frontiers, etc. The Policía Nacional polices urban areas, and there are also municipal and regional" 0.0920 0.9082 0.5432 0.5597 0.5596 0.0165 0.0051 0.3092 0.0771)
  ("police forces like the Basque Ertzaintza and the Catalan Mossos d’Esquadra. Latin-American" 0.0920 0.9081 0.5597 0.5762 0.5761 0.0165 0.0094 0.2640 0.0511)
  ("republics may also have complex policing systems." 0.0920 0.5257 0.5762 0.5927 0.5927 0.0165 0.0048 0.3439 0.0783)
