  ("4 Gender of nouns" 0.0905 0.2404 0.0492 0.0683 0.0679 0.0154 0.0046 0.3029 0.0124)
  ("(2) La presidente ‘president’ is found, but la presidenta is recommended by Seco (1998) and is now" 0.0920 0.9080 0.0832 0.0997 0.0994 0.0165 0.0047 0.3234 0.0225)
  ("very widespread." 0.0920 0.2403 0.0997 0.1162 0.1162 0.0165 0.0048 0.2813 0.0384)
  ("(3) Forms like *la estudianta for la estudiante are considered substandard, but a few popular nouns/" 0.0920 0.9082 0.1284 0.1448 0.1446 0.0165 0.0032 0.3621 0.0225)
  ("adjectives may form their feminine in -nta: el atorrante/la atorranta (Lat. Am.) ‘tramp’/‘slacker’/" 0.0920 0.9081 0.1449 0.1613 0.1613 0.0165 0.0057 0.3600 0.0838)
  ("US ‘bum’, dominanta ‘bossy’/‘pushy’ (applied to women). For la clienta see 1.2.7 note 1." 0.0920 0.8272 0.1614 0.1778 0.1777 0.0165 0.0048 0.3665 0.0251)
  ("1.2.6 Feminine of other nouns in Group A whose masculine form ends" 0.0920 0.9071 0.2019 0.2227 0.2227 0.0208 0.0068 0.3698 0.1731)
  ("in -e or in a consonant" 0.1582 0.4164 0.2220 0.2428 0.2428 0.0208 0.0068 0.3131 0.0216)
  ("Apart from those mentioned in the preceding sections, these do not change:" 0.0920 0.7346 0.2505 0.2670 0.2670 0.0165 0.0048 0.3270 0.0501)
  ("el/la alférez second" 0.1092 0.2607 0.2770 0.2934 0.2933 0.0165 0.0048 0.2544 0.0325)
  ("  lieutenant" 0.1092 0.2143 0.2935 0.3097 0.3097 0.0162 nil 0.2332 0.1051)
