  ("1.3 Group B: Gender of nouns referring to animals not included under 1.2 and to lifeless things 7" 0.1576 0.9088 0.0492 0.0683 0.0679 0.0154 0.0046 0.3586 0.0228)
  ("(to a king), ‘Your Majesty must be tired’. This particularly applies to the phrase su señoría used in" 0.0920 0.9080 0.0832 0.0997 0.0996 0.0165 0.0045 0.3552 0.0232)
  ("the Spanish parliaments to address other members of the two houses and for judges." 0.0920 0.8102 0.0997 0.1162 0.1162 0.0165 0.0048 0.3375 0.0267)
  ("(2) La pareja is used even for a male partner, but note su pareja es español (El Periódico, Sp., 8-3-15)" 0.0920 0.9080 0.1284 0.1448 0.1446 0.0165 0.0047 0.3118 0.0225)
  ("‘her (male) partner is Spanish’. Compañero/compañera are also used for unmarried partners," 0.0920 0.9080 0.1449 0.1613 0.1613 0.0165 0.0088 0.2564 0.0334)
  ("sometimes clarified by adding sentimental, but pareja is becoming more common." 0.0920 0.7750 0.1614 0.1778 0.1777 0.0165 0.0048 0.3814 0.0912)
